{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 31, :comments ["The reason for <b>and you shall keep My commandments</b>: here He admonishes Israel to keep the commandments, that they be scrupulous concerning the offerings with regard to blemishes, and those lacking their required time before seven days, and the day on which the mother is slaughtered, and to prepare the sacrifices and the thanksgiving offering and to slaughter them for acceptance, and He includes all the commandments together. Now He has already mentioned above, among the statutes and the ordinances, \"and you shall keep all My statutes and all My ordinances\" (Leviticus 19:37). And He said, \"neither shall you profane My holy name,\" lest there be among you one who acts deceptively and slaughters a blemished offering to HaShem, as He said concerning the sons of Aaron, \"and they shall not profane My holy name\" (Leviticus 22:2), where He admonished concerning the offerings regarding impurity or blemishes."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:58:08.132853828Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}